{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_paper_architecture", "label": "Paper Architecture \u2014 Restructuring Specification", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Specification only; every proposal is a gate item and no prose was changed in the session that produced it."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_word_limit_scope_ruling", "label": "Resolved Scope of the Word Limit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Abstract and captions count; references and appendices do not. Consequence: appendix space is free, so a DEMOTE is a real saving rather than a relocation of cost, and the CUT/DEMOTE boundary was redrawn on that basis."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_target_tree", "label": "The Target Six-Chapter Tree with Word Budgets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_current_state_inventory", "label": "Current-State Inventory \u2014 37,471 Words Against 20,000", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a word-count problem with a document attached: 187 per cent of the limit with the argument's two load-bearing chapters missing."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_classification_codes", "label": "KEEP / REFRAME / DEMOTE / CUT Classification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_run_log_residue", "label": "Run-Log Residue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chronological accounts of what was tried, debugging narrative, session/phase/audit references, tooling commentary, superseded findings \u2014 anything whose subject is the conduct of the work rather than its result."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_heading_naming_convention", "label": "Heading Naming Convention N1-N8", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A heading that states the finding asks the reader to accept it before seeing any evidence; the finding goes in the first sentence under the heading instead."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_caption_convention", "label": "Caption Convention \u2014 15-Word Title, 45-Word Body", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Current captions average 107 words and read as sentences; anything longer than the cap is prose that has been evicted from the body."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_float_placement_test", "label": "Float Placement Test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A table earns body space only if a reader must look up exact values to follow the argument; a table that demonstrates a pattern, records a sweep or documents a configuration goes to an appendix."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_sec_res_basis_relocation", "label": "The sec:res-basis Relocation into Methods 3.2", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is a methodological decision about the instrument taken before any accuracy figure can be read; reporting it in Results as a finding is what forces every downstream table to explain which ruler it is on."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_thirty_eight_prj93_passages", "label": "Thirty-Eight Passages Reporting PRJ93 Results in Chapter 2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A review of prior work that already contains the results has no gap left to motivate the method."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_remove_excise_relocate", "label": "REMOVE / EXCISE / RELOCATE Dispositions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The EXCISE items are the dangerous ones: a cited claim and a PRJ93 observation are welded into one sentence, so deleting the sentence takes a load-bearing citation with it. Split the sentence; do not delete it."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_gap_from_prior_work_alone", "label": "The Gap Chapter 2 Must Establish from Prior Work Alone", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_seven_gap_limbs", "label": "The Seven Gap Limbs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_entailment_breaks", "label": "Seven Breaks in the Current Order's Entailment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_rubric_map", "label": "Rubric Map \u2014 Criteria per Target Section", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_approvals_a1_a17", "label": "Approvals A1-A17, Closed to Later Sessions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A later session may implement but may not reopen; where it believes an approved item is wrong it raises the conflict rather than revising silently."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_unlock_rows", "label": "Items Reopened After Approval (U1-U5)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A closed-approvals section edited without a trail stops being useful, so a reopening is recorded with its authority and its reason."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_composition_method", "label": "Composition Method \u2014 Compose from Evidence, Not Edit Down", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retained material must reach 61 per cent of its length while changing what it argues; editing preserves the sentence structure of a draft written to a different plan, and a sentence built to carry three clauses does not become a one-clause sentence by deletion."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_reasoning_loss_risk", "label": "Reasoning-Loss Risk in Chapters 2 and 3", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Their evidence bases record verdicts and numbers, not argument; several rejected-alternative reasons exist nowhere but the current prose, and that is precisely the material carrying D7."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_w1_winkler_numerics_sensitivity", "label": "W1 \u2014 tab:winkler Set Membership Is Numerics-Sensitive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A perturbation too small to move a point estimate can still cross alpha and delete a set member; the Winkler means, coverage figures and Clopper-Pearson limbs are all identical across regimes."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_w2_unstamped_mcs_exposure", "label": "W2 \u2014 tab:mcs Inherits the Mechanism and Has Never Been Tested", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gap stays open and is not to be closed by assertion; testing it means regenerating the ladder, which the approved disposition puts out of scope."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_e1_ellel_traded_only_null", "label": "E1 \u2014 Ellel's Traded-Only Limb Is Not Significant", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exchangeability finding is a decomposition, not a trend; dropping the traded-only p-value leaves a true, uninformative statement that is not what was established."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_e2_false_open_limbs_not_a_pair", "label": "E2 \u2014 The Two False-Open Limbs Are Not a Matched Pair", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_a_namespace_collision", "label": "The Four-Way A-Namespace Collision and Its Repair", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rename escapes a collision only if the destination is checked, and checking the destination was the one step the original repair skipped."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_quickwordcount_removal", "label": "Removal of \\quickwordcount from main.tex", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_paper_architecture", "target": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_word_limit_scope_ruling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/knowledge/05_paper_architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_paper_architecture", "target": "brain_knowledge_05_paper_architecture_target_tre